      "claim": "Class: other (wrong person-facing remedy). Where: metasystem/internal/steward/revive.go. The unit adds an hourly stop for steward starts: two or more steward sessions that ended without progress in the rolling hour, across any subjects, block the next start. The stop's message tells the person that 'metasystem machine revive' is the remedy, but that verb cannot clear it. The revive path closes the completed launch and clears only the abnormal-restart slots in the evidence file. The stop is counted from the seat records, which the revive leaves unchanged. So after the person acts, the next tick refuses again with the same remedy, for up to an hour, while the revive's own reply promises that 'the steward's next tick starts the next ready goal'. This also contradicts the design (D1, scenario S3): 'a new occurrence starts again'. With this stop in place, a new subject inside the hour does not start, and the per-occurrence cap of three can only be reached across more than an hour. In U3a no steward session can record progress yet (that comes in U3b), so any two steward sessions within an hour trigger this. Change: either drop the hourly count over steward no-progress records, so that a different subject is a different start as it is for goals (fix by subtraction; the per-occurrence counter already limits repeats), or name a remedy that clears what it counts.",
      "evidence": "Traced path. (1) revive.go:477-485: for start.Kind == \"steward\", ended counts records with Kind steward, StartedAt within the hour and Outcome SeatNoProgress; at ended >= 2 it returns abnormalRemedy(root, \"two automatic abnormal restarts were attempted in the rolling hour\"), which appends \"person's remedy: metasystem machine revive <root>\" (revive.go:449-451). (2) seatDecision returns this as ActNotify (seat_start.go:511-516). (3) The person runs machine revive. ReviveSeat calls startSeatWithDependencies with person proof (seat_start.go:580-587). The last record is a steward session whose launch state is terminal 'completed', so seat_start.go:750-752 calls closeUnboundLaunch(... \"it ended completed, not failed\"). (4) closeUnboundLaunch (seat_start.go:666-682) resets only ev.Abnormal and ev.AbnormalCount and writes no seat record. Its error text says 'the steward's next tick starts the next ready goal'. (5) On the next tick, revive.go:478-483 counts the same seat records, ended is still >= 2, and the same notify with the same remedy returns until the records are an hour old. The new test 'two subjects keep the rolling hour limit' (seat_ladder_test.go) asserts this stop for a third different ask, which is the opposite of S3's 'a new occurrence starts again'.",
